    <GaugingStation location="Mill Croft" name="Abhainn Roag" number="106003">
        <Comments>
            <Comment type="Station Summary">Velocity area station gauging a natural mountainous catchment on South Uist (Outer Hebrides).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Hydrometric">No cableway. Gauged to around QMED. One peak flow rating across period of record.</Comment>
            <Comment type="General">Open channel section 7m wide with gravel control. Station added to peak flows dataset in October 2018 (WINFAP Files v7).</Comment>
            <Comment type="Catchment">A natural mountainous catchment on North Uist with little storage. Mainly rough grazing, peat bog and moorland with some forestry.</Comment>
            <Comment type="Factors affecting runoff"/>
        </Comments>
        <Usages>
            <Usage notes="Gauged up to around QMED." suitable="Yes" type="QMED"/>
            <Usage notes="Not gauged sufficiently above QMED to a sufficient stage to have some confidence in the AMAX 3 event being within 30% of the true value." suitable="No" type="Pooling"/>
        </Usages>
    </GaugingStation>
